 "about": "Aulaga and sweet and bitter tabaiba scattered over the plains, the old lava and the cinder, a few cardones on the old massifs; canary palms by the farms and in the barrancos, tamarisk in the barrancos and on the coastal flats; prickly pears in the old cochineal fields and by the farms, agaves on the terraces, vines in the walled ash pits of La Geria; Majorera goats everywhere, dromedaries at Timanfaya and on the farms of Fuerteventura. The highland cow stands in for the dromedary, and the Canarian house for the white cubic flat-roofed houses with green or brown woodwork.",
